1
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:10,135
<i>Since the majority of players</i>
<i>did not choose greater good,</i>

2
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:13,430
<i>the prize token cannot be obtained.</i>

3
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:14,889
- We didn't get it?
- For real?

4
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:16,182
That's unbelievable.

5
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,351
Is this a prank?

6
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:19,894
- Who was it?
- Let's see it.

7
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:21,604
Dong-jae.

8
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,023
- Dong-min.
- Kyung-lyul.

9
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,024
Jin-ho?

10
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:25,358
Jin-ho?

11
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,737
- Jin-ho?
- Jin-ho?

12
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,823
Turns out he was the one.

13
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:37,245
Seeing myself in last place on that board
was just so irritating.

14
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>As soon as the options appeared on screen,</i>
<i>I pressed option two.</i>

15
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:41,833
I'll choose one.

16
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:43,710
- Did you press it?
- Yes.

17
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:44,711
That makes six, right?

18
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:46,588
Someone could be lying.

19
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:48,840
He didn't lie that much on <i>The Genius.</i>

20
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:50,717
Hong Jin-ho has changed.

21
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,218
We need to teach Jin-ho a lesson.

22
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,012
This won't do, Jin-ho.

23
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:57,557
If he had just looped me in,

24
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,393
<i>we could've secured the prize money,</i>
<i>and I would've helped him out.</i>

25
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:02,103
That damn punk.

26
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,230
He needs to get it together.

27
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,901
And just like that,
we've dropped to the bottom.

28
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:10,320
Jin-ho had no reason to go for option one.

29
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:13,198
- So, we're at the worst-case scenario?
- That's right.

30
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>The third mini-game will now be revealed.</i>

31
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:18,787
<i>The third mini-game of Either Or is</i>

32
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,205
<i>Lay the Grass.</i>

33
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:21,289
<i>In Lay the Grass,</i>

34
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:26,628
<i>players will place their grass tiles</i>
<i>on the park board to earn points.</i>

35
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:31,007
<i>The park board consists of 114 squares,</i>

36
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:36,471
<i>and the grass tiles come in seven types,</i>
<i>each made up of multiple squares.</i>

37
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:39,015
<i>Starting with the player</i>
<i>with the lowest score,</i>

38
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:42,268
<i>each player will publicly select</i>
<i>one grass tile.</i>

39
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:43,645
<i>In the event of a tied score,</i>

40
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:47,690
<i>the player with the higher</i>
<i>priority ranking will go first.</i>

41
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:51,486
<i>Players may select</i>
<i>the same grass tile as another player.</i>

42
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:53,321
<i>Once selected,</i>

43
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:56,908
<i>a grass tile cannot be changed</i>
<i>until the end of the game.</i>

44
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:59,702
<i>Once all players have selected</i>
<i>their grass tiles,</i>

45
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:03,206
<i>they will take turns placing the tiles</i>
<i>on the park board.</i>

46
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:04,541
<i>Players will take turns placing tiles,</i>

47
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:07,293
<i>starting with the player</i>
<i>with the lowest-numbered tile.</i>

48
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,170
<i>If players have the same tile number,</i>

49
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:12,841
<i>the player with the higher</i>
<i>priority ranking will go first.</i>

50
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:14,759
Priority ranking is a big deal here.

51
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:16,427
<i>When placing the grass tiles,</i>

52
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:20,098
<i>players may not flip them over.</i>

53
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:21,224
There won't be enough space.

54
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,768
<i>Players who successfully place</i>
<i>a grass tile</i>

55
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:26,813
<i>will earn points</i>
<i>equal to the number of the tile.</i>

56
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:29,941
<i>Players who fail to place a grass tile</i>

57
00:02:30,024 --> 00:02:32,402
<i>will earn no points.</i>

58
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:37,365
<i>The game will conclude once all players</i>
<i>have had a chance to place their tiles.</i>

59
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:41,077
<i>We will now begin the fifth selection.</i>

60
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,329
I'm sick of making choices already.

61
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:48,042
<i>Players who choose points</i>
<i>will earn five points immediately.</i>

62
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:49,794
<i>Players who choose intel</i>

63
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:53,256
<i>will get to see the options</i>
<i>for the next three selections</i>

64
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:55,592
<i>in the dealer room.</i>

65
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:58,094
- Next options, huh?
- Five points is a lot though.

66
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:00,180
I went so far as to lie earlier

67
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,765
<i>to get those five points</i>
<i>and move up a bit in the rankings.</i>

68
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:05,143
At the very least,
I need to score enough points

69
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:07,228
to keep from slipping in the rankings.

70
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,939
Choosing to acquire advanced intel
in a game like this

71
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:12,525
<i>is a bit meaningless since it always</i>
<i>ends up being shared anyway.</i>

72
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:16,154
What's with the holes?

73
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,281
Nothing was mentioned
about the holes yet, right?

74
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:22,202
POINTS: ACQUIRE 5 POINTS
INTEL: PREVIEW OF 6TH, 7TH, 8TH SELECTIONS

75
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:24,078
You should choose option one.
I'll choose two.

76
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:28,958
I thought alliances
might play a major role in this game.

77
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:29,959
Team Greater Good?

78
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:32,086
Choose option one. I'll choose two.

79
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:35,882
<i>Those who chose greater good earlier</i>
<i>came to mind first.</i>

80
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:38,801
It wasn't because I felt bad
or some sort of idealistic sentiment.

81
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,845
I just think they're people I can trust.

82
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:43,932
- I can't prevent ending up in prison.
- It's unavoidable.

83
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,934
But I can at least try to
prevent elimination.

84
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:48,061
Those who chose greater good
should look out for one another.

85
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,854
- We need to stick together now.
- Yeah.

86
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:52,732
I think those guys
have formed Option One Club.

87
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:54,651
The Greater Good Alliance? Club?

88
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,030
<i>Since I chose personal gain,</i>

89
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:01,908
I assumed those who chose greater good
wouldn't welcome me.

90
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:05,495
So I figured that even if I'm on my own,

91
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:08,665
<i>the intel would give me a better shot</i>
<i>at the main match.</i>

92
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:11,334
- Let's say you get first place.
- Okay.

93
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:15,129
Is there someone you'd save from prison
if they ended up there?

94
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:18,758
Honestly,

95
00:04:18,841 --> 00:04:21,469
XITSUH and you are the only ones
I've discussed that possibility with.

96
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,179
- XITSUH and me?
- Yeah.

97
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,138
We talked earlier.

98
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:26,432
- So we can't both end up there.
- That's right.

99
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:28,434
I'm sure I'm not the only one

100
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:32,188
Dong-min wants by his side.

101
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,482
When it comes to intel,
we just need one person.

102
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:35,942
Who could do that for us?

103
00:04:36,025 --> 00:04:37,944
- Whoever has the lowest tile number
- Yes?

104
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:41,823
- takes the first turn, right?
- Yes.

105
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:45,118
That means there's a chance you might not
be able to place at all later in the game.

106
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,035
Right.

107
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,246
There must be some sort of gimmick
with the holes.

108
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:50,915
- The intel must be about that, the holes.
- Yeah.

109
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,333
We do need intel.

110
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:55,128
<i>I decided not to go for getting intel.</i>

111
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:58,840
<i>Kyung-lyul is desperate</i>
<i>for first place right now,</i>

112
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:02,010
<i>so he'll definitely pick points</i>
<i>over intel.</i>

113
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:04,512
Intel? Who needs it?

114
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:05,596
I'll be fine.

115
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,974
If I just sit tight,
it'll find its way to me anyway.

116
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:11,102
- Who's gonna choose intel?
- What?

117
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,395
Who's gonna choose intel?

118
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:13,396
Me.

119
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:15,106
- You're giving up the five points?
- Yeah.

120
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:16,482
What are you getting in return?

121
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:17,400
Nothing.

122
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:19,652
And who are you sharing the intel with?

123
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,321
Everyone on Team Greater Good.

124
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:22,697
- Team Greater Good?
- Yeah.

125
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:23,614
Why would you do that?

126
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:25,325
That's half the players.

127
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:27,160
It's still an influence game.

128
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:30,204
Then can you share
that intel with me as well?

129
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:34,876
If Dong-min wanted to,
he could easily get that intel.

130
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,002
He would find a way.

131
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:38,880
He could easily have someone else get it

132
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:40,923
<i>after promising</i>
<i>to make it worth their while.</i>

133
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,633
I'll share it with just Dong-min.

134
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:44,260
Is that okay?

135
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:46,679
- Just Dong-min--
- Let me talk to him.

136
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:49,515
Hey.

137
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:54,937
Honestly, I'm not against sharing intel
with Hyun-min or you.

138
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:59,942
But both of you have separate alliances,
so it might end up diluting its value.

139
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,486
The way I see it,

140
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:04,655
strength is in numbers.

141
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:05,656
- Right.
- In numbers.

142
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,992
If you bring me the intel

143
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:11,662
and let me know
who's pulling together right now,

144
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,414
then I'll work out a plan

145
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:17,377
to push everyone outside that group
further down the rankings.

146
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:20,254
<i>In all the survival programs</i>
<i>I've seen Dong-min in,</i>

147
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:21,464
<i>he always kept his word.</i>

148
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:25,510
I also noticed that he's really good
at influence games with multiple players.

149
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:27,178
I'm gonna choose intel anyway,

150
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:29,514
and Dong-min is gonna
get that intel somehow anyway,

151
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:31,474
so I believe our needs line up.

152
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:33,893
Then I'll also pass
that intel along to you.

153
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,019
Okay, great.

154
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:36,896
- Please keep all eight of us in mind.
- I will.

155
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:39,982
<i>All players</i>
<i>have completed their selections.</i>

156
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,694
<i>Here are the players' current scores</i>
<i>based on their selections.</i>

157
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,613
- That's quite a boost.
- No more minus points.

158
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:47,031
Oh no. I'm in last place.

159
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:50,493
<i>XITSUH and Yi Do, you have chosen intel.</i>

160
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:53,246
<i>Please make your way to the dealer room</i>
<i>to review the intel.</i>

161
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,624
Hello.

162
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,960
You should've chosen option two now too.

163
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:00,837
Option one was too good
to give up this time.

164
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:05,925
The upcoming selections will be revealed
for the next five minutes.

165
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:10,930
As long as there are no hidden rules,

166
00:07:11,013 --> 00:07:14,517
- tile 3 seems to be the way to go.
- Yeah.

167
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,477
- And if everyone goes for three? Right.
- Yeah.

168
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,396
Then only about seven people
can place the grass tiles.

169
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:19,981
They can cause chaos with three.

170
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:22,024
If someone does that,

171
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:23,734
- it'll be over after four moves.
- Right.

172
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,945
There's a way to cause
trouble with tile 3,

173
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:27,989
so there must be a hidden rule
to prevent that.

174
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:32,702
<i>Choosing a lower-numbered tile</i>
<i>means first in turn.</i>

175
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:34,871
<i>The player can then stake out their space</i>

176
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:38,291
<i>and disrupt the players</i>
<i>who place later than them.</i>

177
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,170
<i>Choosing a higher-numbered tile</i>
<i>guarantees more points.</i>

178
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:46,466
<i>But if a player's order comes too late,</i>
<i>there may be no space left.</i>

179
00:07:47,175 --> 00:07:51,137
<i>It is a matter of placing early</i>
<i>and claiming a spot</i>

180
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,055
<i>or holding out for a higher score.</i>

181
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:57,101
<i>And the answer</i>
<i>might just lie in that intel.</i>

182
00:07:57,852 --> 00:07:59,812
Please leave the dealer room.

183
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:00,730
Okay.

184
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,024
They're back.

185
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:04,192
Was there a lot?

186
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,777
Holy moly. I nearly wrote my hand off.

187
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:10,698
<i>- Lay the Grass will begin in 20 minutes.</i>
- In 20 minutes?

188
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:12,325
- Let's go.
- Team Greater Good.

189
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:13,826
- Team Fools.
- Team Greater Good.

190
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,578
So those who chose personal gain
are excluded?

191
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,330
That's right. You can ask Yi Do.

192
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:20,500
Does this have anything to do with
your long talk with Dong-min earlier?

193
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:23,628
I'll be discussing my deal with him
with them as well.

194
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:24,962
Just give me a sneak peek.

195
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:25,963
No.

196
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:31,344
Look, I may have looked like a pushover
up until now, but I'm a bulldozer now.

197
00:08:31,427 --> 00:08:34,138
- But you'd need more people anyway.
- That's true.

198
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:37,266
I just haven't figured out
what I want in exchange.

199
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,768
But I will need people on my side.

200
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,353
- Then you need to figure it out.
- Right.

201
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,565
Do you just wanna join us now?

202
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:46,984
- Time is of the essence.
- Sure.

203
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:49,362
But why did you agree to share?
Did he offer a deal?

204
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:51,864
Okay, since everyone is here,

205
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,950
- let me do a quick rundown.
- Hello, Mr. Jang.

206
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:55,034
Hey.

207
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:57,245
- Are they officially a team now?
- Yeah.

208
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,829
They're Team Greater Good now.

209
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,456
Really?

210
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,124
<i>As soon as I left the dealer room,</i>

211
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:06,504
XITSUH and Team Greater Good
went off to discuss the intel.

212
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:08,965
That's when I realized I was screwed.

213
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:11,384
<i>Intel is only valuable</i>
<i>when just a few people have it,</i>

214
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:13,386
but now over half the players
will have it.

215
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:17,306
Then I thought about
how to exclude some people

216
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,058
from having access to it.

217
00:09:19,141 --> 00:09:21,936
<i>I didn't really wanna share it</i>
<i>with a lot of people.</i>

218
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,771
I'm really sorry,

219
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:27,817
but I only really wanna share
all the intel with these two.

220
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,068
- I'm really sorry.
- Okay.

221
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:30,486
- Then…
- We can leave.

222
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:33,281
- We'll discuss it and then…
- So after that?

223
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,657
- Understood.
- Let's hurry. There's no time.

224
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:35,950
We'll get out quickly.

225
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:38,244
But can you two promise me
that you won't betray me?

226
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:41,747
- I won't as long as I'm not in danger.
- I'm happy to help.

227
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,332
I'm actually fine with just three points.

228
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:46,419
Dong-min, why did you come to us
and not them?

229
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:50,840
I was originally planning
to choose greater good as well.

230
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:54,051
But when Kyung-lyul told me
he chose option two,

231
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:58,264
- I had no choice but to choose option two.
- To maintain your first place.

232
00:09:58,347 --> 00:10:00,433
I was always with you guys at heart.

233
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:02,310
Of course, you're the closest
to winning the prize money.

234
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:05,354
- I told XITSUH before I chose as well.
- He did.

235
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:07,732
<i>The reasoning did make sense.</i>

236
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:09,191
<i>And since the top two players</i>

237
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:12,987
<i>retained their ranks</i>
<i>but didn't join forces,</i>

238
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:14,363
I just didn't question it.

239
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:19,160
I was in awe of Dong-min's play
from the very beginning.

240
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:20,828
<i>I'm sure everyone was happy to have him.</i>

241
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:22,913
- Let's all take a look at this.
- Okay.

242
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:25,333
I have terrible handwriting,
so let me just read it.

243
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:29,253
<i>These are the three selections</i>
<i>that were revealed to XITSUH and Yi Do.</i>

244
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:31,964
<i>First, attack or defend.</i>

245
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:33,466
- I'll explain it quickly.
- Okay.

246
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:35,551
The sixth selection
is between attack and defend.

247
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:38,846
"If attack is chosen,
successful tile placement

248
00:10:38,929 --> 00:10:41,641
will double the tile number in points."

249
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,685
"Failure to place
will result in a four-point deduction."

250
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:49,315
If you choose defend, you can cut
up to two squares from your tile.

251
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:52,443
A protruding part like this
can just be cut off.

252
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:55,613
If you wanna cut off two squares,
they must be connected.

253
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,031
- They <i>have to </i>be connected.
- Yeah.

254
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:58,991
And it can't be a square with a number.

255
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,994
And the tile can't be separated into two.

256
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:03,871
Is it an individual or majority vote?

257
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:05,706
- Individual.
- Got it.

258
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:06,832
Each player decides.

259
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,877
Next is mutual benefit or rivalry.

260
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,922
<i>The seventh selection</i>
<i>is between mutual benefit and rivalry.</i>

261
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,216
"If mutual benefit is chosen,
two players team up."

262
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:19,720
"When their tiles are adjacent,
each shared side earns a bonus point."

263
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,430
So if three sides are touching,
that's three points?

264
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:22,348
- Exactly.
- Okay.

265
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:24,767
"Bonus points are distributed
by mutual agreement."

266
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,686
"If rivalry is chosen,
the player wins five bonus points

267
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,271
if there are nine or fewer tiles
on the park board, including their own."

268
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,857
Basically, you want everyone to fail
except for yourself.

269
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:33,234
Now, the eighth selection.

270
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:34,819
Tree or manholes.

271
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:37,238
<i>The eighth selection</i>
<i>is between a tree and manholes.</i>

272
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:39,490
You must have a hole for the tree,
no matter what.

273
00:11:39,573 --> 00:11:41,409
- Common sense.
- So you can keep others away.

274
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:43,661
You're basically placing obstacles
on the field.

275
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,037
- So you get to plant them.
- Yes.

276
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:47,832
There are +1 and -1 manholes.

277
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:51,460
So, placing a grass tile on a manhole
adds or deducts one point.

278
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:54,922
The order is as follows.
Manholes, tree, and grass tile.

279
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:55,923
The placement order.

280
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:59,719
Since manholes are placed first,
you can place them to stop trees.

281
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,303
They can't coexist in the same spot.

282
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:03,639
- So no trees on top of manholes?
- Yes, because manholes are placed first.

283
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:05,641
<i>When it comes to selecting tiles,</i>

284
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:10,312
<i>players cannot afford to overlook</i>
<i>trees and manholes.</i>

285
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,148
<i>The placement of trees</i>

286
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:17,361
<i>undeniably limits the placement</i>
<i>of lower-numbered tiles without holes.</i>

287
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,780
Since we outnumber them,

288
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:22,908
they won't be able to put together
a disruption strategy involving trees.

289
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:26,036
Since Yi Do has the lowest score,

290
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,956
as long as we keep a close eye on her,

291
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:32,376
I believe we can avoid
someone on our team being eliminated.

292
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,503
<i>Since she'll be choosing first,</i>

293
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:39,508
<i>it's unlikely that she'll choose</i>
<i>the higher numbers like 9, 11, and 13.</i>

294
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:43,929
Since the lower-numbered tiles
have zero to a few holes,

295
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,557
we can strategically use the trees

296
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,684
to prevent scoring.

297
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:53,147
If Yi Do picks tile 9 or 11,

298
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:55,232
we can assume her team
is going for points.

299
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:59,195
Then we can select tile 9

300
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:02,448
and cut the bottom two
for a defensive strategy.

301
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:05,659
We should be able to place all our tiles
if we just have five squares.

302
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:08,078
Tiles 7, 9, and 11
could all end up with 5 squares.

303
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:08,996
- Plenty of holes too.
- Yeah.

304
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:12,541
Tile 9 has 3 holes
and offers a lot of points.

305
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,710
- But that's not the case for tile 11.
- It's too wide.

306
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,962
The five squares
are spread out horizontally,

307
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:18,380
so that will be a bit of a gamble.

308
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:22,009
Tile 9 is the way to go
to score big and play it safe.

309
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:24,512
- We have two possible strategies.
- I get it.

310
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:26,972
It just depends
on what Yi Do ends up choosing.

311
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:33,854
Strategy-wise, we first need to figure out
who we need from that group.

312
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:36,273
More people knowing
doesn't exactly benefit us.

313
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:37,900
But to come up with a better strategy,

314
00:13:37,983 --> 00:13:39,860
we should bring in Dong-jae or Hyun-min

315
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:42,780
- to think this through.
- I agree.

316
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,534
Come in.

317
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:48,577
- We need to strategize.
- We do.

318
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:49,703
- Okay.
- So…

319
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:51,747
Yi Do, have you decided?

320
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:53,374
When did they get here?

321
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,125
Can we come in now?

322
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:58,420
Can we share the intel with them?

323
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,172
You can decide, Yi Do.

324
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:02,258
There were three selections
that I saw in advance.

325
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:05,719
But out of the three, what would impact
the other players the most

326
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,221
