- Sure.

655
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:13,882
This will be our goal.

656
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:15,925
Is there a way to block tile 6?

657
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:17,969
To keep others away.

658
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:19,304
- I'll plant it here.
- Okay.

659
00:27:20,263 --> 00:27:23,266
<i>Players will now start</i>
<i>placing the grass tiles.</i>

660
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:26,728
<i>Jung Won-young, please place</i>
<i>your grass tile on the park board.</i>

661
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,147
Wherever it fits.

662
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:33,276
Found one.

663
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,111
- Good.
- That's a good one.

664
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:38,239
- Wait. I can just go over them.
- Yeah.

665
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:43,036
- This was what we wanted earlier.
- Yeah, that's best.

666
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:44,579
Okay.

667
00:27:45,789 --> 00:27:48,249
Will we get interfered with or not?

668
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:50,502
Jung Won-young
has successfully placed his tile.

669
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:53,588
You have placed it over
one -1 tile and one +1 tile,

670
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:54,923
- so no bonus points will be awarded.
- Okay.

671
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:57,133
Next, Yurisa. Please place your tile.

672
00:27:57,217 --> 00:27:58,259
Go, Yurisa.

673
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:01,096
I have a few options.

674
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:03,765
If we can deter while building, great.

675
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:07,352
Nice.

676
00:28:07,435 --> 00:28:09,104
Tile 7 can be placed there, right?

677
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:10,563
Try it.

678
00:28:10,647 --> 00:28:12,023
I think it can be placed like this.

679
00:28:12,107 --> 00:28:13,983
- It fits.
- Does it?

680
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,360
- It won't work.
- It's pointless, then.

681
00:28:15,443 --> 00:28:16,653
To stop me?

682
00:28:16,736 --> 00:28:18,738
Then this spot would be better.

683
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:21,032
- Over here, maybe?
- Yeah.

684
00:28:21,116 --> 00:28:23,493
- Like this?
- There are a lot of -1 tiles here.

685
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:26,496
You can either prevent mutual benefit
or take up space

686
00:28:26,579 --> 00:28:28,957
to stop others from placing
and stop rivalry.

687
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,834
It's up to you.

688
00:28:30,917 --> 00:28:33,670
- You can block that area if you want.
- Okay.

689
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:35,213
Hyun-gyu planted a tree here

690
00:28:35,296 --> 00:28:38,299
so they could go in and stop us.

691
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:40,135
Considering that,

692
00:28:40,218 --> 00:28:43,722
taking this area to thwart their plan
kind of appeals to me.

693
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:47,434
Is it a bad idea to just place it
without considering mutual benefit?

694
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:49,561
- What about the points?
- Why give that up?

695
00:28:49,644 --> 00:28:52,939
If we give that up
and reduce available space,

696
00:28:53,022 --> 00:28:55,400
- we can stop others from scoring.
- Even more?

697
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:57,944
- That's possible.
- That's another way to get a point gap.

698
00:28:58,027 --> 00:28:59,904
But then what about the people
who chose mutual benefit?

699
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:03,032
This applies to them as well.

700
00:29:03,116 --> 00:29:04,909
- Stopping others from scoring--
- In a way,

701
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:07,287
you're looking to cause a bit of chaos
and skip mutual benefit.

702
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:08,788
- Like this?
- Yeah.

703
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:13,460
<i>Hong Jin-ho and Yurisa stand to earn</i>
<i>five points from mutual benefit.</i>

704
00:29:13,543 --> 00:29:16,087
<i>But if they place</i>
<i>their tiles apart as shown,</i>

