901
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:19,927
<i>In Memory Poker,</i>
<i>players will memorize 16 cards,</i>

902
00:36:20,011 --> 00:36:24,682
<i>then form the strongest possible hand</i>
<i>using the shared cards.</i>

903
00:36:24,765 --> 00:36:28,352
<i>When the game begins,</i>
<i>16 cards will be randomly revealed</i>

904
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:33,107
<i>from a deck of 52 plain cards</i>
<i>for 20 seconds.</i>

905
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:36,611
<i>Afterward, the three shared cards</i>
<i>will be revealed.</i>

906
00:36:36,694 --> 00:36:41,157
<i>Players must choose two cards</i>
<i>from the sixteen they memorized</i>

907
00:36:41,240 --> 00:36:45,578
<i>that form the strongest possible hand</i>
<i>when combined with the three shared cards.</i>

908
00:36:45,661 --> 00:36:46,746
Oh, I see.

909
00:36:46,829 --> 00:36:48,206
Basically looking for nuts.

910
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:51,834
<i>Players will select their two cards</i>

911
00:36:51,918 --> 00:36:56,255
