<i>by the two lowest-ranked players</i>

937
00:37:56,816 --> 00:37:58,776
<i>and will be played</i>
<i>as a winning-streak game.</i>

938
00:37:59,652 --> 00:38:01,445
<i>The two lowest-ranked players</i>

939
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:03,864
<i>will face off</i>
<i>against the higher-ranked players</i>

940
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:05,825
<i>on a one-on-one basis.</i>

941
00:38:05,908 --> 00:38:07,660
You have to win your way up to survive.

942
00:38:07,743 --> 00:38:12,665
<i>Memory Poker will be the final opportunity</i>
<i>for players to turn their fate around.</i>

943
00:38:12,748 --> 00:38:15,584
<i>Here are the players' current rankings.</i>

944
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:17,169
It's a match against Yi Do.

945
00:38:17,253 --> 00:38:18,379
NUCKSAL, YI DO

946
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:23,384
<i>Tied scores were broken</i>
<i>by priority ranking.</i>

947
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:25,177
The guys at the top
are out of this entirely.

948
00:38:25,261 --> 00:38:28,806
<i>Before the game begins,</i>
<i>we will begin the tenth selection.</i>

949
00:38:28,889 --> 00:38:32,435
<i>If eight or more players</i>
<i>choose the challenge method,</i>

950
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:36,689
<i>players in 15th and 16th place</i>
<i>may each challenge 1 higher-ranked player</i>

951
00:38:36,772 --> 00:38:39,859
<i>to face in the winning-streak game.</i>

952
00:38:39,942 --> 00:38:41,986
<i>The 15th-place player will go first,</i>

953
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:45,948
<i>followed by the 16th-place player.</i>

954
00:38:46,032 --> 00:38:50,077
<i>A win will advance the player</i>
<i>one spot in the rankings.</i>

955
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:53,497
<i>The losing player</i>
<i>will drop one place in the rankings,</i>

956
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:56,834
<i>swapping positions</i>
<i>with the player directly below them.</i>

957
00:38:56,917 --> 00:38:59,628
<i>After winning,</i>
<i>the 15th- or 16th-place player</i>

958
00:38:59,712 --> 00:39:02,757
<i>will challenge a new,</i>
<i>higher-ranked opponent</i>

959
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:04,592
<i>to keep the winning-streak game going.</i>

960
00:39:04,675 --> 00:39:09,096
<i>However, a player cannot challenge</i>
<i>the same opponent twice.</i>

961
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:11,849
<i>If the challenged player wins,</i>

962
00:39:11,932 --> 00:39:13,642
<i>they will earn one Piece.</i>

963
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:18,189
<i>If nine or more players</i>
<i>choose the ladder method,</i>

964
00:39:18,272 --> 00:39:20,107
<i>the 15th- and 16th-place players</i>

965
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:22,401
<i>will compete against the player</i>
<i>ranked directly above them</i>

966
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:24,445
<i>in a winning-streak game.</i>

967
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:28,324
<i>Each win will move the player up</i>
<i>one place,</i>

968
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:31,035
<i>and they will continue</i>
<i>the winning-streak game against the player</i>

969
00:39:31,118 --> 00:39:32,828
<i>now directly above them.</i>

970
00:39:33,621 --> 00:39:35,831
<i>- In both methods,</i>
- That's brutal.

971
00:39:35,915 --> 00:39:38,542
<i>if the 15th- or 16th-place player loses,</i>

972
00:39:38,626 --> 00:39:41,545
<i>their winning streak will come to an end.</i>

973
00:39:41,629 --> 00:39:46,175
<i>If a new player drops to 15th</i>
<i>or 16th place following a match,</i>

974
00:39:46,258 --> 00:39:48,344
<i>they will take over</i>
<i>as the next participant</i>

975
00:39:48,427 --> 00:39:49,804
<i>in the winning-streak game.</i>

976
00:39:51,013 --> 00:39:53,224
Wait, then how many rounds are there?

977
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:57,186
<i>The game will conclude when no new players</i>

978
00:39:57,269 --> 00:39:59,355
<i>- drop to 15th or 16th place.</i>
- So we keep going?

979
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:03,317
<i>However, if a player who previously held</i>
<i>15th or 16th place moved up</i>

980
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:05,986
<i>and then dropped back to 15th or 16th,</i>

981
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:08,447
<i>they will not be considered a new player.</i>

982
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:14,787
<i>Now, please choose either</i>
<i>the challenge method or ladder method</i>

983
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:17,081
<i>using the devices.</i>

984
00:40:17,164 --> 00:40:18,416
Challenge method, obviously.

985
00:40:18,499 --> 00:40:19,834
