1396
01:03:08,618 --> 01:03:10,953
So you can just choose whoever you want.

1397
01:03:14,957 --> 01:03:17,335
Can you tell us who you have in mind?

1398
01:03:18,169 --> 01:03:19,003
Am I one of them?

1399
01:03:19,504 --> 01:03:21,297
Hong Jin-ho in seventh place,

1400
01:03:21,380 --> 01:03:22,632
assume the push-up position.

1401
01:03:25,551 --> 01:03:28,930
I discussed it with them,

1402
01:03:29,013 --> 01:03:30,765
and I've decided to respect their wishes.

1403
01:03:30,848 --> 01:03:32,141
I'll give it to Oh Hyun-min.

1404
01:03:33,518 --> 01:03:36,229
- I'm sick of that Jang-Oh Alliance.
- My goodness.

1405
01:03:36,312 --> 01:03:40,399
- I thought he'd choose XITSUH.
- That bond is unbreakable.

1406
01:03:40,483 --> 01:03:42,068
<i>I actually wanted to save XITSUH.</i>

1407
01:03:42,151 --> 01:03:47,365
<i>But I feel like both of them</i>
<i>would come back out alive either way.</i>

1408
01:03:47,448 --> 01:03:50,076
When XITSUH said what he did,

1409
01:03:50,159 --> 01:03:52,203
I expected Hyun-min
to just volunteer to go.

1410
01:03:52,286 --> 01:03:55,206
<i>But the fact that he didn't,</i>
<i>even after what XITSUH said,</i>

1411
01:03:55,289 --> 01:03:58,501
made me think that, for whatever reason,
Hyun-min must not be confident today.

1412
01:03:58,584 --> 01:04:02,004
<i>Oh Hyun-min</i>
<i>will be going to the living area.</i>

1413
01:04:02,088 --> 01:04:06,801
<i>The players for both the living area</i>
<i>and the prison have been decided.</i>

1414
01:04:06,884 --> 01:04:10,596
<i>Players will be rewarded with Pieces</i>
<i>based on the final results.</i>

1415
01:04:10,680 --> 01:04:13,349
<i>The players who chose</i>
<i>performance bonus in the first selection</i>

1416
01:04:13,432 --> 01:04:16,394
<i>- and managed to end up in the living area</i>
- Right, I forgot about this.

1417
01:04:16,477 --> 01:04:19,438
<i>are Jang Dong-min, Yurisa,</i>
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul, and Oh Hyun-min.</i>

1418
01:04:19,522 --> 01:04:21,232
<i>They will all be rewarded with one Piece.</i>

1419
01:04:21,315 --> 01:04:22,733
I also chose the living area, damn it.

1420
01:04:25,361 --> 01:04:26,445
Unbelievable.

1421
01:04:26,529 --> 01:04:27,905
I even got this wrong.

1422
01:04:29,031 --> 01:04:30,408
I'm so pissed.

1423
01:04:30,491 --> 01:04:32,702
You need to face reality.

1424
01:04:32,785 --> 01:04:34,662
I'm on the cut line.

1425
01:04:34,745 --> 01:04:35,788
Seriously.

1426
01:04:35,872 --> 01:04:38,666
<i>The players who chose insurance payout</i>
<i>in the first selection</i>

1427
01:04:38,749 --> 01:04:43,671
<i>and ended up in prison are Jeong Hyun-gyu,</i>
<i>XITSUH, and Stella Jang.</i>

1428
01:04:43,754 --> 01:04:45,381
<i>They will all be rewarded with two Pieces.</i>

1429
01:04:45,464 --> 01:04:47,717
Hyun-gyu, you predicted prison?

1430
01:04:47,800 --> 01:04:49,343
- Yes.
- Really?

1431
01:04:50,177 --> 01:04:53,472
<i>Now, please make your way</i>
<i>to your respective living spaces.</i>

1432
01:04:54,098 --> 01:04:57,685
<i>Players going to prison,</i>
<i>please head down the stairs on the left.</i>

1433
01:04:58,311 --> 01:05:00,479
- Sorry.
<i>- Players going to the living area,</i>

1434
01:05:00,563 --> 01:05:03,524
- Don't worry about it.
<i>- please head up the stairs on the right.</i>

1435
01:05:03,608 --> 01:05:05,693
<i>To be honest, I'm not entirely at ease.</i>

1436
01:05:05,776 --> 01:05:10,948
So I'm gonna do whatever it takes
to be of help to XITSUH

1437
01:05:11,032 --> 01:05:13,868
and to be the best teammate tomorrow.

1438
01:05:13,951 --> 01:05:15,202
Get some rest.

1439
01:05:15,870 --> 01:05:16,704
Good luck.

1440
01:05:16,787 --> 01:05:18,080
See you later.

1441
01:05:18,164 --> 01:05:19,415
Jin-ho.

1442
01:05:19,498 --> 01:05:20,333
Good luck.

1443
01:05:21,375 --> 01:05:22,835
- You're dead when I get back.
- Come to your senses.

1444
01:05:22,919 --> 01:05:24,170
Be prepared.

1445
01:05:24,253 --> 01:05:25,421
Pull yourself together, Jin-ho.

1446
01:05:25,504 --> 01:05:26,631
Good luck.

1447
01:05:30,676 --> 01:05:32,929
- Get some rest.
- Let's go.

1448
01:05:33,012 --> 01:05:34,472
- Prisoners!
- Good job today!

1449
01:05:34,555 --> 01:05:35,765
- Let's go.
- Good luck, prisoners.

1450
01:05:35,848 --> 01:05:36,933
- All right.
- Good job, everyone.

1451
01:05:37,016 --> 01:05:39,602
- Bye.
- For the sin of choosing the greater good.

1452
01:05:40,227 --> 01:05:41,646
Oh my gosh.

1453
01:05:41,729 --> 01:05:44,148
You must hand in your personal belongings.

1454
01:05:44,231 --> 01:05:45,775
They're not allowed inside.

1455
01:05:45,858 --> 01:05:47,610
- Is there food inside?
- I don't have anything.

1456
01:05:50,571 --> 01:05:52,114
It's nice and cozy.

1457
01:05:52,198 --> 01:05:53,240
Hey, it's nice.

1458
01:05:53,324 --> 01:05:55,409
It's not like prisons elsewhere.
It's nice.

1459
01:05:55,493 --> 01:05:56,661
There's even a bathroom.

1460
01:05:56,744 --> 01:05:57,745
Wow.

1461
01:05:58,579 --> 01:05:59,580
Wow.

1462
01:06:00,373 --> 01:06:02,375
Wow!

1463
01:06:04,251 --> 01:06:05,503
- What the heck?
- What's that?

1464
01:06:06,837 --> 01:06:07,797
What?

1465
01:06:07,880 --> 01:06:08,923
- What?
- It's all out in the open?

1466
01:06:10,049 --> 01:06:11,884
Oh, this is it?
We're all sleeping together.

1467
01:06:11,968 --> 01:06:14,095
- This is nice.
- Isn't it?

1468
01:06:14,178 --> 01:06:17,098
But there's no privacy at all.

1469
01:06:17,181 --> 01:06:18,683
It's just all open now.

1470
01:06:19,600 --> 01:06:20,434
Wait.

1471
01:06:20,518 --> 01:06:22,478
- What's that?
- Seriously?

1472
01:06:22,561 --> 01:06:23,688
- What the heck?
- Are they serious?

1473
01:06:23,771 --> 01:06:25,272
- We can see each other.
- What is this?

1474
01:06:25,356 --> 01:06:26,816
- Come on.
- We can?

1475
01:06:26,899 --> 01:06:29,110
- What is this?
- My gosh.

1476
01:06:29,193 --> 01:06:31,779
It's like the last car in <i>Snowpiercer.</i>

1477
01:06:31,862 --> 01:06:35,282
Damn, this is so cruel.
What on earth is this?

1478
01:06:35,366 --> 01:06:37,326
Damn it.

1479
01:06:37,410 --> 01:06:40,037
This is a bit too much.
We can see them sleeping.

1480
01:06:40,121 --> 01:06:42,581
- Man, this is insane.
- This is on a new level.

1481
01:06:42,665 --> 01:06:44,166
- This is something else.
- This is brutal.

1482
01:06:44,750 --> 01:06:46,794
I don't wanna go down there.

1483
01:06:46,877 --> 01:06:49,005
I don't ever wanna go down there.

1484
01:06:49,088 --> 01:06:50,715
- This is just crazy.
- I wanna live here forever.

1485
01:06:51,424 --> 01:06:53,384
- This is so irritating.
- So annoying.

1486
01:06:53,467 --> 01:06:56,095
- This is like <i>Parasite</i>.
- They can look down.

1487
01:06:59,140 --> 01:07:00,516
The ceiling was made of glass,

1488
01:07:00,599 --> 01:07:04,895
so the players in the living area
said hello to us.

1489
01:07:04,979 --> 01:07:07,690
We looked up and said hello.

1490
01:07:07,773 --> 01:07:09,025
It was super annoying.

1491
01:07:09,817 --> 01:07:11,277
Human nature is never satisfied.

1492
01:07:11,360 --> 01:07:13,320
I wanna spend at least a day
in the living area.

1493
01:07:14,113 --> 01:07:18,743
<i>Players in prison,</i>
<i>please change into the provided outfits.</i>

1494
01:07:18,826 --> 01:07:22,204
<i>The prison match will begin at 8:30 p.m.</i>

1495
01:07:22,288 --> 01:07:25,124
<i>Until then, spend the time as you wish.</i>

1496
01:07:25,207 --> 01:07:26,250
Let's get changed first.

1497
01:07:26,333 --> 01:07:27,168
Prison uniform.

1498
01:07:27,251 --> 01:07:28,461
They even have indoor shoes.

1499
01:07:28,544 --> 01:07:29,837
There are T-shirts too.

1500
01:07:30,337 --> 01:07:31,881
There are socks in here too.

1501
01:07:31,964 --> 01:07:33,841
- Socks? Very good.
- Nice.

1502
01:07:33,924 --> 01:07:36,093
- This is intense.
- Wait, are we sleeping all together?

1503
01:07:36,177 --> 01:07:37,386
- All in one room?
- Everything's here.

1504
01:07:37,470 --> 01:07:39,597
Then where are we supposed to scheme?

1505
01:07:39,680 --> 01:07:41,057
Can't we just scheme here together?

1506
01:07:43,225 --> 01:07:44,393
Wow, nice.

1507
01:07:45,936 --> 01:07:47,980
We can eat now, right?

1508
01:07:48,064 --> 01:07:49,273
- It's nice.
- I need some water.

1509
01:07:49,356 --> 01:07:50,191
Me too.

1510
01:07:50,816 --> 01:07:52,902
- Kelly and Terra? Love those.
- Thank you.

1511
01:07:52,985 --> 01:07:54,070
I'm starving right now.

1512
01:07:54,153 --> 01:07:55,654
Hey, there are snacks too.

1513
01:07:55,738 --> 01:07:59,909
<i>Players in the living area,</i>
<i>please change into the provided outfits.</i>

1514
01:07:59,992 --> 01:08:01,327
- Where are they?
- Where are they?

1515
01:08:07,958 --> 01:08:09,126
Do these come in one size?

1516
01:08:09,210 --> 01:08:10,544
No, there are different sizes.

1517
01:08:10,628 --> 01:08:11,587
This is nice.

1518
01:08:12,630 --> 01:08:13,756
Not bad at all.

1519
01:08:17,802 --> 01:08:20,805
Is that the bread we're supposed to share?

1520
01:08:20,888 --> 01:08:21,972
Our main meal.

1521
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:24,725
Oh, it's milk.

1522
01:08:24,809 --> 01:08:26,602
Bread and milk? It could be worse.

1523
01:08:26,685 --> 01:08:28,270
The players in prison in Season 2

1524
01:08:28,354 --> 01:08:30,189
- just kept losing weight.
- Yeah.

1525
01:08:30,272 --> 01:08:31,315
A serious detox.

1526
01:08:31,398 --> 01:08:33,609
Their faces grew more gaunt by the day.

1527
01:08:35,402 --> 01:08:37,530
Wow, look up there.

1528
01:08:37,613 --> 01:08:39,323
Look at those carts of delicious food.

1529
01:08:40,324 --> 01:08:41,534
What's that?

1530
01:08:42,201 --> 01:08:43,410
What's all that?

1531
01:08:43,494 --> 01:08:44,829
It's our meal.

1532
01:08:44,912 --> 01:08:45,913
Sweet.

1533
01:08:45,996 --> 01:08:47,081
That looks so tasty.

1534
01:08:47,164 --> 01:08:47,998
Yeah, let's eat.

1535
01:08:49,125 --> 01:08:51,544
I'm not jealous in the slightest.

1536
01:08:54,880 --> 01:08:56,966
They're eating right above our heads.

1537
01:08:57,508 --> 01:09:00,094
There are pig's trotters
and lettuce wraps.

1538
01:09:00,177 --> 01:09:01,137
Pig's trotters?

1539
01:09:01,220 --> 01:09:03,597
You can't crave what you've never had,

1540
01:09:03,681 --> 01:09:05,933
but since we've gotten a taste of this,
let's just stay here.

1541
01:09:06,016 --> 01:09:07,268
That'd be so nice.

1542
01:09:07,351 --> 01:09:09,228
Should we just keep this group going?
It's nice.

1543
01:09:09,311 --> 01:09:12,231
But at least one person
has to be eliminated tomorrow.

1544
01:09:12,314 --> 01:09:14,984
- Do you wanna go?
- It's usually the one who says it.

1545
01:09:15,067 --> 01:09:16,777
- I'm screwed.
- I said nothing.

1546
01:09:18,028 --> 01:09:20,322
Thank goodness I'm not down there.

1547
01:09:20,406 --> 01:09:21,699
- It looked like they got
- Oh dear.

1548
01:09:21,782 --> 01:09:24,618
some rye bread and milk.

1549
01:09:35,171 --> 01:09:37,089
How can it taste so bland?

1550
01:09:37,173 --> 01:09:41,343
You get a full view of the living area
when you lie down.

1551
01:09:41,427 --> 01:09:42,928
- Really?
- That's annoying.

1552
01:09:43,012 --> 01:09:46,015
- They're so happily enjoying their meal.
- Are they?

1553
01:09:48,225 --> 01:09:50,352
I just locked eyes with Dong-jae.

1554
01:10:02,698 --> 01:10:05,701
Dong-jae, you sent them down there,
and now you're conversing with them?

1555
01:10:05,784 --> 01:10:07,244
My heart could still go out to them.

1556
01:10:07,328 --> 01:10:08,913
Spill some pig's trotters down there.

1557
01:10:10,414 --> 01:10:11,582
So cruel.

1558
01:10:15,586 --> 01:10:16,754
There has to be something here.

1559
01:10:16,837 --> 01:10:18,464
- But it doesn't seem like it.
- Yeah.

1560
01:10:18,547 --> 01:10:19,381
There's nothing.

1561
01:10:19,465 --> 01:10:20,549
I wonder why.

1562
01:10:20,633 --> 01:10:22,343
Where would you even hide
a device in here?

1563
01:10:22,426 --> 01:10:24,386
- You're right.
- It's such an open space.

1564
01:10:24,470 --> 01:10:27,056
Last time, they had a few rooms.

1565
01:10:27,139 --> 01:10:30,434
Maybe we can open that floor
like a window and go down.

1566
01:10:32,853 --> 01:10:35,272
<i>Everyone knows</i>

1567
01:10:35,356 --> 01:10:38,484
there's always a hidden stage
somewhere in <i>The Devil's Plan.</i>

1568
01:10:38,567 --> 01:10:42,404
So I thought there might be something.
I was on <i>Great Escape</i>, after all.

1569
01:10:42,905 --> 01:10:45,157
<i>I have experience</i>
<i>in digging through rooms.</i>

1570
01:10:45,658 --> 01:10:48,869
<i>I searched really hard because</i>
<i>if anyone should find a clue, it's me.</i>

1571
01:10:55,960 --> 01:10:59,171
We're just searching everywhere
for the hidden stage

1572
01:10:59,255 --> 01:11:00,673
or just a clue about it.

1573
01:11:00,756 --> 01:11:06,095
It seems like everyone's eager
to find something,

1574
01:11:06,178 --> 01:11:08,639
<i>but we haven't found anything yet.</i>

1575
01:11:09,974 --> 01:11:11,350
Look at them walking around again.

1576
01:11:11,433 --> 01:11:13,352
They must be searching for something.

1577
01:11:16,772 --> 01:11:18,816
- Maybe there's something here.
- There must be, right?

1578
01:11:20,442 --> 01:11:22,987
I assume they hid it really well.

1579
01:11:23,070 --> 01:11:24,655
There's physically no space.

1580
01:11:24,738 --> 01:11:26,657
Nowhere to crawl into.

1581
01:11:28,033 --> 01:11:29,451
There must be something.

1582
01:11:32,288 --> 01:11:34,915
Maybe we have to tap on something
for something to pop up

1583
01:11:34,999 --> 01:11:36,750
from inside these pipes or something.

1584
01:11:36,834 --> 01:11:38,877
Should we flip the mattresses over
to start?

1585
01:11:39,712 --> 01:11:42,381
What if we do, and Pieces just spill out?

1586
01:11:44,550 --> 01:11:46,635
- There's nothing.
- Wait, what's this?

1587
01:11:47,177 --> 01:11:48,220
There's nothing.

1588
01:11:50,639 --> 01:11:53,851
We thought there really might be
something in prison.

1589
01:11:53,934 --> 01:11:57,229
There was no sign
of any hidden mechanism whatsoever.

1590
01:11:57,313 --> 01:11:59,398
I guess I was a little disappointed.

1591
01:11:59,481 --> 01:12:01,900
I don't even have the energy
to search today.

1592
01:12:01,984 --> 01:12:03,485
I know. Aren't you exhausted?

1593
01:12:03,569 --> 01:12:05,738
Why did I walk into this hell willingly?

1594
01:12:07,031 --> 01:12:08,282
You two are new to this, right?

1595
01:12:08,365 --> 01:12:09,575
- That's right.
- Yes.

1596
01:12:10,159 --> 01:12:12,536
How could they treat
all these winners like this?

1597
01:12:12,619 --> 01:12:16,582
The winners of Season 1 and Season 2
and <i>The Genius </i>are all here.

1598
01:12:16,665 --> 01:12:18,667
What were they thinking? I'm so mad.

1599
01:12:18,751 --> 01:12:20,711
I'm the only one
who would get eliminated in this bunch.

1600
01:12:20,794 --> 01:12:22,463
Come on, we should still try our best.

1601
01:12:22,546 --> 01:12:24,089
I will.

1602
01:12:24,173 --> 01:12:26,800
Better to get it over with.
Consider this your tour of prison.

1603
01:12:26,884 --> 01:12:28,761
The living area will be even sweeter now.

1604
01:12:29,428 --> 01:12:31,430
Based on what I've seen
in Seasons 1 and 2,

1605
01:12:32,056 --> 01:12:33,349
it's hard to leave this place.

1606
01:12:33,432 --> 01:12:34,641
But isn't it different this time?

1607
01:12:34,725 --> 01:12:36,935
For all we know, the game tomorrow

1608
01:12:37,019 --> 01:12:38,562
- could completely turn things around.
- True.

1609
01:12:38,645 --> 01:12:42,566
And I'm sure they also have
their fair share of cracks to work on.

1610
01:12:42,649 --> 01:12:47,279
After all, they all chose
personal gain earlier.

1611
01:12:47,363 --> 01:12:48,364
You think so?

1612
01:12:48,447 --> 01:12:50,699
Everyone here chose greater good,
except Jin-ho.

1613
01:12:51,325 --> 01:12:52,659
The sin of choosing greater good.

1614
01:12:52,743 --> 01:12:54,870
Sorry, but let's not focus
on a trivial matter.

1615
01:12:54,953 --> 01:12:56,538
Why stir up internal conflict now?

1616
01:12:56,622 --> 01:12:57,664
It's important.

1617
01:12:58,332 --> 01:13:00,876
- We trust each other…
- Did anyone up there choose greater good?

1618
01:13:00,959 --> 01:13:02,961
- Won-young and?
- Just him.

1619
01:13:03,754 --> 01:13:05,506
Everybody else chose personal gain.

1620
01:13:05,589 --> 01:13:07,383
Yeah, I should pursue
my own interests too.

1621
01:13:08,300 --> 01:13:09,635
That's your conclusion?

1622
01:13:09,718 --> 01:13:11,637
Too bad we lost the 100 million won
in prize money.

1623
01:13:11,720 --> 01:13:13,055
Tell me about it.

1624
01:13:13,138 --> 01:13:14,723
It's at zero now, right?

1625
01:13:14,807 --> 01:13:16,100
We can start earning tomorrow.

1626
01:13:16,600 --> 01:13:19,061
Some of us are worried
about even having a tomorrow.

1627
01:13:19,144 --> 01:13:21,814
- We're all mentally there.
- Of course.

1628
01:13:21,897 --> 01:13:23,774
- We're just not making it obvious.
- Absolutely.

1629
01:13:24,525 --> 01:13:26,151
I wonder what the prison match will be.

1630
01:13:26,235 --> 01:13:29,321
It's the first one, so I have no clue.

1631
01:13:29,405 --> 01:13:30,906
I hope it's not another memory game.

1632
01:13:31,698 --> 01:13:33,283
What are you most confident in, XITSUH?

1633
01:13:33,367 --> 01:13:34,410
Freestyle rap.

1634
01:13:35,828 --> 01:13:37,913
- A rap battle would be nice.
- I know, right?

1635
01:13:37,996 --> 01:13:39,540
Any kind of word game would be nice.

1636
01:13:40,124 --> 01:13:41,375
Stella's quite the rapper too.

1637
01:13:42,751 --> 01:13:43,836
- Me?
- She'll take second place.

1638
01:13:43,919 --> 01:13:45,587
So there was a worthy rival, huh?

1639
01:13:46,547 --> 01:13:48,048
I should be more humble.

1640
01:13:49,383 --> 01:13:50,217
Oh jeez.

1641
01:13:51,093 --> 01:13:52,052
It's eight o'clock.

1642
01:13:52,678 --> 01:13:53,637
What's that?

1643
01:13:53,720 --> 01:13:54,638
"In a few moments…"

1644
01:13:54,721 --> 01:13:58,392
<i>The prison match will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

1645
01:13:58,475 --> 01:14:00,144
<i>In today's prison match,</i>

1646
01:14:00,227 --> 01:14:02,104
<i>two players will be eliminated</i>

1647
01:14:02,187 --> 01:14:04,064
<i>- and leave </i>The Devil's Plan.
- What?

1648
01:14:04,148 --> 01:14:05,232
- Two people?
- Two?

1649
01:14:05,899 --> 01:14:06,984
- Are you serious?
- Two?

1650
01:14:07,067 --> 01:14:08,235
Two people?

1651
01:14:08,735 --> 01:14:11,447
<i>The first prison match</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan <i>is</i>

1652
01:14:11,530 --> 01:14:13,323
<i>Heavy 13.</i>

1653
01:14:13,407 --> 01:14:14,658
What's that about?

1654
01:14:14,741 --> 01:14:19,872
<i>In Heavy 13, players must use cards</i>
<i>to add a load to each bearer's stand</i>

1655
01:14:19,955 --> 01:14:23,333
<i>but keep the total of their numbers</i>
<i>below 13 to avoid penalty points.</i>

1656
01:14:23,417 --> 01:14:28,380
<i>Each player will be given seven rock cards</i>
<i>numbered zero to six,</i>

1657
01:14:28,464 --> 01:14:31,884
<i>two chips each in red, green, and blue,</i>

1658
01:14:31,967 --> 01:14:34,511
<i>and one rainbow chip.</i>

1659
01:14:35,095 --> 01:14:36,388
<i>In Heavy 13,</i>

1660
01:14:36,472 --> 01:14:41,143
<i>there are three bearer stands,</i>
<i>in red, green, and blue.</i>

1661
01:14:41,226 --> 01:14:44,605
<i>Players will take turns</i>
<i>using rock cards and color chips</i>

1662
01:14:44,688 --> 01:14:47,149
<i>to load rocks onto the stands.</i>

1663
01:14:47,232 --> 01:14:48,108
Rocks?

1664
01:14:48,192 --> 01:14:52,029
<i>As Hong Jin-ho had the highest ranking</i>
<i>in the main match,</i>

1665
01:14:52,112 --> 01:14:55,908
<i>he will start Round 1</i>
<i>holding the first-player marker.</i>

1666
01:14:56,533 --> 01:14:59,203
<i>Players will be given three minutes</i>

1667
01:14:59,286 --> 01:15:03,457
<i>to secretly submit one rock card</i>
<i>and one color chip.</i>

1668
01:15:03,540 --> 01:15:07,419
<i>The color chip indicates</i>
<i>which bearer's stand the rock will go on,</i>

1669
01:15:07,503 --> 01:15:12,174
<i>and the number on the rock card determines</i>
<i>the weight of the rock cube to be placed.</i>

1670
01:15:12,799 --> 01:15:16,178
<i>Once submissions are complete,</i>
<i>the color chips will be revealed first,</i>

1671
01:15:16,261 --> 01:15:18,222
<i>then the rock cards.</i>

1672
01:15:18,305 --> 01:15:19,765
<i>Based on the result,</i>

1673
01:15:19,848 --> 01:15:22,935
<i>the order in which players</i>
<i>place their rock cubes will be determined.</i>

1674
01:15:23,018 --> 01:15:23,894
Rock cubes.

1675
01:15:23,977 --> 01:15:27,981
<i>We will now explain</i>
<i>how the placement order is determined.</i>

1676
01:15:28,065 --> 01:15:31,568
<i>The players who submit their rainbow chip</i>

1677
01:15:31,652 --> 01:15:33,570
<i>will go first.</i>

1678
01:15:34,321 --> 01:15:40,494
<i>Then the player who submitted</i>
<i>the higher-number rock card will go next.</i>

1679
01:15:40,577 --> 01:15:44,331
<i>If players have submitted rock cards</i>
<i>with the same number,</i>

1680
01:15:44,414 --> 01:15:48,252
<i>the player holding</i>
<i>the first-player marker will go next.</i>

1681
01:15:48,877 --> 01:15:53,340
<i>When players share the same rank</i>
<i>under the above criteria,</i>

1682
01:15:53,423 --> 01:15:56,093
<i>order will be decided clockwise</i>

1683
01:15:56,176 --> 01:15:58,512
<i>from whoever holds</i>
<i>the first-player marker.</i>

1684
01:15:59,137 --> 01:16:00,973
<i>Once the placement order is decided,</i>

1685
01:16:01,056 --> 01:16:04,268
<i>the dealer will place the rock cubes</i>
<i>on the corresponding bearer's stand</i>

1686
01:16:04,351 --> 01:16:07,980
<i>based on each player's</i>
<i>submitted color chip and rock card.</i>

1687
01:16:08,063 --> 01:16:09,439
So they're taking turns stacking it.

1688
01:16:09,523 --> 01:16:12,568
<i>If a player submits a rainbow chip,</i>

1689
01:16:12,651 --> 01:16:15,862
<i>they may choose</i>
<i>whichever bearer's stand they wish.</i>

1690
01:16:16,780 --> 01:16:20,409
<i>When the rock cubes are being placed,</i>

1691
01:16:20,492 --> 01:16:23,954
<i>each player will be allowed</i>
<i>one pass per round.</i>

1692
01:16:24,037 --> 01:16:26,206
<i>A player who passes</i>

1693
01:16:26,290 --> 01:16:28,875
<i>will have their rock cube placed last,</i>

1694
01:16:28,959 --> 01:16:30,627
<i>after all other rock cubes</i>
<i>have been placed.</i>

1695
01:16:31,420 --> 01:16:34,172
<i>If multiple players pass,</i>

1696
01:16:34,256 --> 01:16:37,718
<i>placement will proceed in reverse order</i>
<i>of their passes.</i>

1697
01:16:38,343 --> 01:16:41,972
<i>In other words, the first player to pass</i>

1698
01:16:42,055 --> 01:16:43,890
<i>will be last to place their rock cube.</i>

1699
01:16:44,558 --> 01:16:46,685
<i>During placement of the rock cubes,</i>

1700
01:16:46,768 --> 01:16:50,230
<i>if the sum of rock cubes</i>
<i>on a bearer's stand</i>

1701
01:16:50,314 --> 01:16:53,609
<i>reaches 13 or more</i>
<i>due to a newly placed cube,</i>

1702
01:16:53,692 --> 01:16:55,569
<i>all cubes on that stand will be collected,</i>

1703
01:16:55,652 --> 01:16:58,905
<i>and the player responsible</i>
<i>will receive penalty points</i>

1704
01:16:58,989 --> 01:17:00,449
<i>equal to the number of cubes collected.</i>

1705
01:17:01,408 --> 01:17:05,037
<i>The cube that triggered the collection</i>

1706
01:17:05,120 --> 01:17:07,331
<i>will stay on the stand.</i>

1707
01:17:08,165 --> 01:17:12,002
<i>When all players have placed their cubes,</i>
<i>the round will end,</i>

1708
01:17:12,085 --> 01:17:14,463
<i>and the last player</i>
<i>to receive penalty points</i>

1709
01:17:14,546 --> 01:17:16,006
<i>will become the first player.</i>

1710
01:17:16,757 --> 01:17:18,383
<i>At the end of Round 7,</i>

1711
01:17:18,467 --> 01:17:21,553
<i>each player will be given</i>
<i>another set of rock cards and color chips</i>

1712
01:17:21,637 --> 01:17:22,846
<i>with the same composition.</i>

1713
01:17:23,472 --> 01:17:25,849
<i>The rock cubes</i>
<i>already on the bearer's stands</i>

1714
01:17:25,932 --> 01:17:28,226
<i>will not be reset at this point,</i>

1715
01:17:28,310 --> 01:17:31,396
<i>and the game will resume as is.</i>

1716
01:17:31,480 --> 01:17:35,484
<i>The game will proceed</i>
<i>the same way up to Round 14.</i>

1717
01:17:35,984 --> 01:17:36,943
Round 14?

1718
01:17:37,027 --> 01:17:39,071
<i>When the game ends,</i>
<i>final rankings will be decided</i>

1719
01:17:39,154 --> 01:17:43,575
<i>by each player's total penalty points</i>
<i>from the collected rock cubes.</i>

1720
01:17:43,659 --> 01:17:47,913
<i>The player with the most penalty points</i>
<i>will be ranked last.</i>

1721
01:17:47,996 --> 01:17:50,082
<i>If penalty points are tied,</i>

1722
01:17:50,165 --> 01:17:54,419
<i>the player who most recently received</i>
<i>penalty points will be ranked lower.</i>

1723
01:17:55,295 --> 01:17:57,506
<i>As a reward, the player in first place</i>

1724
01:17:57,589 --> 01:18:00,217
<i>will receive four Pieces.</i>

1725
01:18:00,801 --> 01:18:02,344
- That many?
- That many?

1726
01:18:02,427 --> 01:18:05,013
<i>If there is a tie for first place,</i>

1727
01:18:05,097 --> 01:18:07,683
<i>the four Pieces</i>
<i>will be split evenly among them,</i>

1728
01:18:07,766 --> 01:18:09,976
<i>and any leftover Pieces will be discarded.</i>

1729
01:18:10,060 --> 01:18:14,773
<i>The sixth- and seventh-place players</i>
<i>will be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

1730
01:18:14,856 --> 01:18:16,733
- Four eliminations today?
- Four?

1731
01:18:16,817 --> 01:18:20,320
<i>The game will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

1732
01:18:20,404 --> 01:18:21,988
I should've begged Dong-min.

1733
01:18:22,739 --> 01:18:24,658
It'll be difficult to count
with seven people.

1734
01:18:24,741 --> 01:18:27,411
- That would be a lot to keep track of.
- Yeah, for sure.

1735
01:18:27,494 --> 01:18:30,580
- But you're good at that.
- The color chips, the cards.

1736
01:18:30,664 --> 01:18:33,041
Yeah, and they won't even let us
write stuff down.

1737
01:18:33,917 --> 01:18:36,420
What's everyone's first card gonna be?

1738
01:18:37,504 --> 01:18:38,463
Rainbow, zero.

1739
01:18:39,047 --> 01:18:40,632
- That's…
- Lies.

1740
01:18:41,174 --> 01:18:42,008
Rainbow…

1741
01:18:42,092 --> 01:18:43,510
- Use it when you're in danger.
- That's…

1742
01:18:43,593 --> 01:18:46,888
- Only when you really need to use it.
- Right.

1743
01:18:46,972 --> 01:18:49,224
So you'd use it when you've only got
green and blue chips left,

1744
01:18:49,307 --> 01:18:51,309
but you need red.

1745
01:18:51,393 --> 01:18:52,269
Exactly.

1746
01:18:52,352 --> 01:18:53,645
It's like a Joker.

1747
01:18:53,729 --> 01:18:56,898
- Zero is something of a one-off relief.
- It's a penalty blocker.

1748
01:18:56,982 --> 01:18:59,693
It's like a Joker or wild card you use
to skip your turn.

1749
01:18:59,776 --> 01:19:01,653
You can pass?

1750
01:19:01,737 --> 01:19:03,947
If you use pass
when you don't wanna place anything,

1751
01:19:04,030 --> 01:19:07,993
you get pushed all the way to the back.

1752
01:19:08,076 --> 01:19:09,619
And if multiple people pass,

1753
01:19:09,703 --> 01:19:11,621
funnily enough,
the last to pass goes first.

1754
01:19:11,705 --> 01:19:13,123
They start again in reverse order.

1755
01:19:13,832 --> 01:19:17,377
So if you pass first,
you actually end up placing last.

1756
01:19:17,461 --> 01:19:21,631
<i>The most important thing in Heavy 13</i>
<i>is the rock cube placement order.</i>

1757
01:19:21,715 --> 01:19:24,968
<i>If cards and color chips</i>
<i>are submitted as shown on screen,</i>

1758
01:19:25,051 --> 01:19:29,264
<i>the player who submitted</i>
<i>the rainbow chip goes first.</i>

1759
01:19:29,347 --> 01:19:32,642
<i>Then, players proceed in order</i>
<i>from the highest rock card number down.</i>

1760
01:19:32,726 --> 01:19:35,103
<i>If rock card numbers are tied,</i>

1761
01:19:35,187 --> 01:19:39,191
<i>the order is then determined</i>
<i>clockwise from the first player.</i>

1762
01:19:39,274 --> 01:19:44,654
<i>During placement,</i>
<i>any player may pass once.</i>

1763
01:19:44,738 --> 01:19:49,534
<i>The player who passes</i>
<i>places their cube last.</i>

1764
01:19:49,618 --> 01:19:52,579
<i>If multiple players pass,</i>

1765
01:19:52,662 --> 01:19:56,041
<i>they place their cubes in reverse order</i>
<i>of the original sequence.</i>

1766
01:19:56,124 --> 01:19:58,585
Also, this first player keeps changing,

1767
01:19:58,668 --> 01:20:00,545
- and their position plays a big role too.
- So true.

1768
01:20:00,629 --> 01:20:02,339
First player must be important.

1769
01:20:03,131 --> 01:20:04,549
I think we just need to try it out.

1770
01:20:04,633 --> 01:20:06,301
- And figure it out as we go.
- Right.

1771
01:20:06,384 --> 01:20:09,095
You need to watch what others do

1772
01:20:09,179 --> 01:20:10,847
and decide on the spot.

1773
01:20:12,474 --> 01:20:13,558
What? Already?

1774
01:20:13,642 --> 01:20:16,686
- It's been 30 minutes already?
- <i>The prison match will begin shortly.</i>

1775
01:20:17,562 --> 01:20:18,730
Guess it's game over for me.

1776
01:20:18,814 --> 01:20:20,941
<i>All players in prison,</i>

1777
01:20:21,024 --> 01:20:25,445
<i>please make your way to the death room</i>
<i>with your Pieces.</i>

1778
01:20:29,825 --> 01:20:30,659
Let's go.

1779
01:20:30,742 --> 01:20:31,701
Let's go.

1780
01:20:36,665 --> 01:20:37,958
This is a really long corridor.

1781
01:20:38,750 --> 01:20:39,960
Something feels off.

1782
01:20:43,922 --> 01:20:45,507
It's so pretty.

1783
01:20:47,717 --> 01:20:48,593
<i>Welcome.</i>

1784
01:20:48,677 --> 01:20:52,556
<i>This is the death room,</i>
<i>where all prison matches will be held.</i>

1785
01:20:53,557 --> 01:20:54,599
<i>The moment I walked in…</i>

1786
01:20:54,683 --> 01:20:58,270
<i>With my life at stake,</i>
<i>I couldn't help but feel intimidated.</i>

1787
01:20:58,353 --> 01:21:00,146
<i>It was quite overwhelming.</i>

1788
01:21:00,230 --> 01:21:01,982
<i>It was surrounded by mirrors.</i>

1789
01:21:02,065 --> 01:21:03,817
- Do we just stand here?
- I think so?

1790
01:21:03,900 --> 01:21:05,235
Can we take any spot?

1791
01:21:05,318 --> 01:21:06,653
Take any spot you wish.

1792
01:21:06,736 --> 01:21:07,696
- Really?
- Is that right?

1793
01:21:09,948 --> 01:21:12,576
<i>I thought that luck would matter</i>
<i>as much as the moves I make,</i>

1794
01:21:12,659 --> 01:21:15,370
<i>and that I actually might survive this.</i>

1795
01:21:15,453 --> 01:21:16,788
<i>It gets real from that point.</i>

1796
01:21:16,872 --> 01:21:18,164
<i>You think, "As long as it's not me,"</i>

1797
01:21:18,248 --> 01:21:19,708
<i>but then realize, "Wait, could it be me?"</i>

1798
01:21:19,791 --> 01:21:21,501
<i>Someone has to leave.</i>

1799
01:21:21,585 --> 01:21:22,419
<i>Two, actually.</i>

1800
01:21:22,502 --> 01:21:26,339
<i>I'm confident</i>
<i>that I'm not gonna be in the bottom two.</i>

1801
01:21:26,423 --> 01:21:27,757
<i>It's totally different.</i>

1802
01:21:27,841 --> 01:21:29,259
<i>The contestants' energy is different.</i>

1803
01:21:29,342 --> 01:21:31,386
<i>They adjusted so quickly too.</i>

1804
01:21:31,469 --> 01:21:33,972
<i>There are so many strong competitors here,</i>

1805
01:21:34,055 --> 01:21:38,226
<i>so I'm gonna stay humble</i>
<i>and do my best to avoid being eliminated.</i>

1806
01:21:38,310 --> 01:21:40,896
<i>They've gathered all the veterans</i>
<i>of survival games here.</i>

1807
01:21:40,979 --> 01:21:42,439
<i>This is so annoying.</i>

1808
01:21:42,522 --> 01:21:47,319
<i>We will now begin the first prison match,</i>
<i>Heavy 13.</i>

1809
01:21:53,575 --> 01:21:56,244
<i>I'm scared. I hate this.</i>

1810
01:21:56,328 --> 01:21:57,871
<i>- Oh no.</i>
<i>- What is that?</i>

1811
01:21:57,954 --> 01:21:59,205
<i>- This is insane.</i>
<i>- Is that a person?</i>

1812
01:21:59,289 --> 01:22:00,665
<i>This is how it's gonna be?</i>

1813
01:22:00,749 --> 01:22:01,958
<i>What is all this?</i>

1814
01:22:02,042 --> 01:22:03,168
<i>When does it end?</i>

1815
01:22:04,419 --> 01:22:06,046
<i>I really hate stuff like this.</i>

1816
01:22:07,464 --> 01:22:08,381
<i>What is all this?</i>

1817
01:22:08,465 --> 01:22:09,424
<i>This is insane.</i>

1818
01:22:09,507 --> 01:22:11,176
<i>- We need to see what it is.</i>
<i>- It's so fishy.</i>

1819
01:23:52,277 --> 01:23:57,282
Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
